// S1a-3 (design 1): the length index of Array[A](n) is the last arg of the interned Array type id: a Len type, kind 7. Its key is EXACT: the
// head is the tag, the raw words of the key are its args (Tp.nargs hides them): tag 0 literal (hi, lo of the value, <= 18 digits),
// 1 binder (file, token), 2 fresh rigid (a counter: equal only to itself), 3 erased (a mono key: no length), 4 hidden binder of a signature
// (a counter; a call replaces it: a param by a length var, a result by a fresh rigid). There is no Any: two lengths are equal iff one id.
def Typer.cLenNN(): I64 = 340
